B.d13=new A.a5("Where it is kept","Your account, and what you write and record, are kept by Supabase, who store the app's data. Your phone tells us which of four broad time-zone bands it is in, and nothing finer; we use it for the night reminder and to hold notifications to anyone not known to be 18 or over between midnight and 6 am.")
B.d_R=new A.a5("Who hears a recording","A room and everything in it is seen only by the people in it, except what somebody there chooses to show others, such as a song they ask a musician to play on or put on the Open Mic.\n\nAnalysing a recording uses our own code at RunPod and Google Cloud to separate the parts, read the chords and hear the words. OpenAI hears a recording when our code gives its sheet no words, or when you ask the sheet to listen for the words again. Our own tests may send stored recordings to OpenAI, RunPod and our chord detector only when everyone on the song has said yes, and you can change your choice under Take part in our tests, in Privacy and safety on Account. Profile, gallery and room pictures and song covers you upload are sent to OpenAI too, to be checked. When the app needs help to answer a question about a song, the question and what the app has worked out about the song go to Anthropic or OpenAI; the recording never does.")
B.d_N=new A.a5("When you delete","Deleting your account leaves some things behind, among them the songs you started and the takes you shared in other people's rooms, without your name, and what our analysis worked out from your recordings.")
B.d1e=new A.a5("Backups","Something you delete can stay in our nightly backups for at least sixty days.")
